OL,3,GNEWSAFire boss thanks staff and public
OL,4,Ain open letter
OL,5,
OL,6,FA fire service chief has thanked
OL,7,Femergency services and communities for
OL,8,Ftheir response to a series of fires
OL,9,Facross the West Midlands.
OL,11,FIn an open letter published on Friday,
OL,12,Fexternal, chief fire officer, Simon
OL,13,FTuhill, said West Midlands Fire Service
OL,14,Freceived thousands of 999 calls on 13
OL,15,FAugust - one of the hottest days of the
OL,16,Fyear.
OL,18,FThe most serious was a large fire in
OL,19,FStourbridge which destroyed 19 homes
OL,20,Fand forced dozens of people to
OL,21,Fevacuate.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,352,350,200,160,0,100
